 explain=["Chandragupta Maurya founded the Mauryan Empire around 321 BCE with the help of his advisor Chanakya, also known as Kautilya. The capital was Pataliputra. The empire grew to include most of the Indian subcontinent.","Ashoka was the most famous Mauryan emperor. After the bloody Kalinga war he felt great sorrow and chose the path of non-violence and dhamma, a code of kindness and moral conduct. He had messages carved on rocks and pillars, called edicts, in the languages and scripts of the people.","The Mauryans had a strong government with officers, a large army, roads and trade. Ashoka's lion capital at Sarnath is India's national emblem."],
